link_device_memory_legacy: yield instead of sleeping on a full ring

When the CP's ring of the boot channel is full while cbd streams the
firmware images, xmit_to_legacy_link() sleeps 50 ms per try. In the DDE
driver, that sleep did not return while the stream ran. The task yields
to the other tasks instead, as tested on the phone.

--- a/src/google_s5300/link_device_memory_legacy.c
+++ b/src/google_s5300/link_device_memory_legacy.c
@@ -304,7 +304,7 @@
 			if (in_interrupt())
 				mdelay(50);
 			else
-				msleep(50);
+				cond_resched();
 			continue;
 		}
 
